vehicle loans, and deposit account overdrafts; and commercial loans. In addition, it provides transaction processing and investment brokerage services. Further, the company engages in the sale of securities and the operation of banking office, lending centers, an operations center, customer call center, administration center, and a wealth management center. Greene County Bancorp, Inc. was founded in 1889 and is based in Catskill, New York. Greene County Bancorp, Inc. operates as a subsidiary of Greene County Bancorp, MHC.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Donald E. Gibson | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 203 people. Revenue per employee of $456K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 10%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $205K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Greene County Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $615M market cap on $93M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 8% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $42M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 45 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.03\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.7%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 58% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5295106070153338},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 21% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 51% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","25 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (GCBC) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.s